<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexandros Zaimis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1855–1936</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexandros Zaimis was a Greek statesman who served several times as prime minister. In 1906 he replaced Prince George as High Commissioner of the autonomous Cretan State, holding the post until 1911 as the island moved towards union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. From 1929 to 1935 he was president of the Second Hellenic Republic, which ended with the restoration of the monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexandros-zaimis.jpg" alt="Alexandros Zaimis" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zaimis37216v.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
